  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed boundary treatment, by reason of its siting, excessive height and design, would result in a visually enclosing development that would detrimentally impact upon the open character and appearance of the existing dwellinghouse. Moreover, due to the positioning of the application site on a prominent corner location, the height and design would appear incongruous and would detract from the openness, character and appearance of Shrewsbury Road and the surrounding area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy 28 of the Sutton Council Plan 2018 and Sutton's Urban Design Guide 'Creating Locally Distinctive Places' SPD (SPD14).",
    "Due to lack of details to the contrary, the proposed development is unacceptable on highway grounds, by reason of its location within close proximity of a T-junction, its excessive height and design. As such, it is considered that highways and pedestrian safety would be adversely affected by the proposal and the proposed development would be contrary to Policy 37 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
